- runtime-core/ is a one-time copy of xiaok-cli commit
  f8728a346ccbed625c5918ffe7f8f8305ebdf7df (src/, desktop/shared,
  desktop/electron, desktop/resources), taken 2026-11-11 (UTC+8).
  KTeam has modified it: former build-time adaptations are baked into the
  source and names, environment variables, data directories and keychain
  service names were changed from xiaok to KTeam. KTeam maintains this copy
  itself and does not sync it with xiaok-cli.
- desktop/core-ui/ (A2UI renderer) derives from xiaok-cli commit
  8f36042e209e0a6fc0c5ffe4b95f4bd9e8eb8056.
- src/core-protocol/room-workspace-protocol.ts and
  src/core-protocol/room-external-discussion.ts derive from xiaok-cli commit
  e385c26508fb942670b8816a92d0044c7bf4ebfc
  (desktop/electron/room-workspace-protocol.ts,
  desktop/shared/room-external-discussion.ts).
- The builtin Skills in desktop/skills (except KTeam's own collaboration
  Skill) derive from xiaok-cli's data/skills; some were edited for KTeam.

KSwarm and intent-broker are reused through semantic service adapters.
Their local source packages are development-only integration dependencies.

AIMP 3.1 and the product design baseline were supplied by the project owner.
Their original text, test-vector provenance and review limitations are retained.

KTeam direct local Agent integration reuses source-pinned KSwarm runtime-capabilities.js, kimi-cli-harness.js and pi-cli-harness.js (Apache-2.0), and the existing Intent Broker participant registration protocol. Native CLI programs remain separately installed and retain their own licenses and configuration.

KTeam bundles kai-report-creator and kai-slide-creator from kai-xiaok-plugins
(https://github.com/kaisersong/kai-xiaok-plugins), Apache-2.0. The pinned revision
and host adaptations are recorded in sources.lock.json under creatorPlugins.
Their Python interpreter and dependency licenses ship inside build/plugins.

KTeam's Windows installation-absence diagnostic in runtime-core/native derives
from xiaok-cli f8728a34 (Apache-2.0). It is maintained as KTeam code and probes
only KTeam's installation namespace; source is compiled with the current build.
